{"edits": [{"finding_ids": ["app/invoices.py:12:config-class"], "search": "from pydantic import BaseModel", "replace": "from pydantic import BaseModel, field_serializer", "explanation": "Add the field_serializer import needed for the v2 replacement of the removed json_encoders setting."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/invoices.py:12:config-class"], "search": "    class Config:
        json_encoders = {
            datetime: lambda v: v.strftime("%Y-%m-%d"),
            Decimal: lambda v: f"{v:.2f}",
        }", "replace": "    @field_serializer("issued_at", when_used="json")
    def _serialize_issued_at(self, v: datetime) -> str:
        return v.strftime("%Y-%m-%d")

    @field_serializer("amount", when_used="json")
    def _serialize_amount(self, v: Decimal) -> str:
        return f"{v:.2f}"", "explanation": "The v1 `class Config` is deprecated and `json_encoders` is deprecated in v2 (migration.md#changes-to-config). Replace it with @field_serializer methods. when_used="json" matches v1 behavior, where json_encoders only applied to JSON output. The same formats are kept for issued_at (%Y-%m-%d) and amount (.2f). No model_config is added because the only config was json_encoders."}, {"finding_ids": ["app/invoices.py:20:deprecated-method"], "search": "    return inv.json()", "replace": "    return inv.model_dump_json()", "explanation": "`.json()` is deprecated in Pydantic v2 (migration.md#changes-to-pydanticbasemodel-3). Use `model_dump_json()`, which produces the same JSON for this model. The field serializers above keep the custom date and decimal formatting."}], "notes": "Config fix: json_encoders is deprecated in v2, and the migration guide says to move config to model_config. Since json_encoders was the only setting, I used @field_serializer(when_used="json") on issued_at and amount. This keeps the same output and is the documented v2 replacement, so no model_config = ConfigDict(...) is needed. Note that json_encoders applied to every datetime and Decimal in the model. Here there are only those two fields, so the per-field serializers are equivalent. The `.json()` call is switched to `model_dump_json()`. The `datetime` and `Decimal` imports are still used by the type hints and the serializers. Nothing else was changed. Not verified by running; the edits are based on static reading of the file."}
